codex
Root cause: the conversion work added three single-line fixtures to `first_path.py`. LCB accepted them, but QBE required newlines. QBE compilation ran only in the macOS native harness. The mutable-width diagnostics were expected rejections.

Fix: corrected fixture formatting and moved QBE compilation outside the macOS gate, so both Linux jobs exercise it. No semantic expectations changed.

Local first-path, mutable-width, conversion, and fuzz tests passed under timeout.

Pushed to `origin/concrete-int-conv` and watched [CI run 42426090869](https://github.com/unbalancedparentheses/lean-compiler-backend/actions/runs/42426090869) through success: **Ubuntu x86, Ubuntu ARM, and macOS 15 all green**, including native Apple ARM64 checks.

